{"step_index":266,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-21T11:35:35Z","input_tokens":228537,"cache_read_tokens":0,"output_tokens":1135,"content":"# 🚀 How to Open the NexusMobility Web Application\n\nThe **NexusMobility** web application is completely self-contained (HTML5, CSS3, Modern JavaScript) with zero required installation or external build steps. You can launch and use it immediately using either method below:\n\n---\n\n### 🌟 Method 1: Instant Direct Launch in Browser (Easiest & Recommended)\n\n1. **Open File Explorer** on your computer.\n2. In the File Explorer address bar, paste this path and press <kbd>Enter</kbd>:\n   ```text\n   C:\\Users\\Kartik Bhosle\\.gemini\\antigravity\\brain\\6976d1a8-fd03-4453-a790-acd552e1861a\n   ```\n3. Locate the file named [**`index.html`**](file:///C:/Users/Kartik%20Bhosle/.gemini/antigravity/brain/6976d1a8-fd03-4453-a790-acd552e1861a/index.html).\n4. **Double-click `index.html`** (or right-click and choose **\"Open with\"** &rarr; **Google Chrome**, **Microsoft Edge**, **Brave**, or **Mozilla Firefox**).\n\n> 💡 **Tip:** You can also click this direct local file link to open it right now in your default browser:\n> 👉 [**Launch NexusMobility (index.html)**](file:///C:/Users/Kartik%20Bhosle/.gemini/antigravity/brain/6976d1a8-fd03-4453-a790-acd552e1861a/index.html)\n\n---\n\n### 💻 Method 2: Launch via Windows Command Prompt / PowerShell\n\n1. Press <kbd>Win</kbd> + <kbd>R</kbd> on your keyboard to open the **Run** dialog.\n2. Type `cmd` and press <kbd>Enter</kbd>.\n3. Copy and paste the following command, then hit <kbd>Enter</kbd>:\n   ```cmd\n   start \"\" \"C:\\Users\\Kartik Bhosle\\.gemini\\antigravity\\brain\\6976d1a8-fd03-4453-a790-acd552e1861a\\index.html\"\n   ```\n   *Your default web browser will immediately pop up displaying the dashboard.*\n\n---\n\n### 🌐 Method 3: Launch with a Local Development Server (Optional)\n\nIf you prefer running through a local web server (e.g. for network inspection):\n\n#### Using Python:\n1. Open Command Prompt and navigate to the folder:\n   ```cmd\n   cd \"C:\\Users\\Kartik Bhosle\\.gemini\\antigravity\\brain\\6976d1a8-fd03-4453-a790-acd552e1861a\"\n   ```\n2. Start Python's built-in server:\n   ```cmd\n   python -m http.server 8000\n   ```\n3. Open your browser and navigate to:\n   ```text\n   http://localhost:8000\n   ```\n\n#### Using VS Code (Live Server extension):\n1. Open the folder in VS Code.\n2. Right-click [`index.html`](file:///C:/Users/Kartik%20Bhosle/.gemini/antigravity/brain/6976d1a8-fd03-4453-a790-acd552e1861a/index.html) and select **\"Open with Live Server\"**.\n\n---\n\n### 🎮 First-Time Operating Tips Once It Opens\n\n1. **One-Click Quickstart**: Click the **\"⚡ Rush-Hour Simulation\"** button in the top navigation bar. This instantly populates:\n   - Driver partners and their 4-seat blueprints.\n   - Live passenger requests in the dispatch pipeline.\n   - Standby passengers in the 5-slot priority ring.\n   - An active trip with animated transit vehicle driving along the 3D map.\n2. **Navigate the Tabs**:\n   - **Tab 1: Eco-Route Finder & Map** &rarr; Select an Origin and Destination station, adjust the Commuter Density Slider, click **\"Calculate Route\"**, and click **\"Drive\"** to watch the vehicle navigate in 3D.\n   - **Tab 2: Commuter Passenger Hub** &rarr; Request a passenger ride, dequeue requests, or push to the 5-Slot Priority Standby Lounge.\n   - **Tab 3: Driver Fleet & Dispatch Console** &rarr; Click the seats in the Top-Down Vehicle Blueprint to toggle availability, onboard drivers, and verify ID numbers (e.g., `#101` or `NX-501`).\n   - **Tab 4: City Sustainability Analytics** &rarr; View environmental impact, carbon offset metrics, and the top eco-partner leaderboard."}
